# Files that stay in this repository and never reach the published snapshot.
#
# `export-ignore` is honoured by `git archive`, which is how the public tree is built. It
# changes nothing about this repository: the files stay tracked, reviewed and in history here,
# and simply do not travel.
#
# Each entry below is internal process documentation or internal tooling. None of it is useful
# to a reader of the published repository, and describing its contents here would defeat the
# point of withholding it, so this file says only that the entry is excluded.

# The publication process itself.
docs/pre-publication-checklist.md export-ignore

# Hosting findings and deployment logistics.
docs/site-deployment.md export-ignore

# The identifier sweep's tooling, which is only useful when run against a live instance of the
# app by whoever operates this repository. Its test ships nowhere either, since a test for an
# absent script is just a broken import.
scripts/collect-identifiers.mjs export-ignore
scripts/collect-identifiers.test.mjs export-ignore

# Internal planning and working discussion (superpowers workflow artifacts). Private by the
# owner's rule (2026-10-25): code and the canonical requirements/design docs are public; the
# AI-assisted plans and specs that worked them out stay private.
docs/superpowers/** export-ignore
docs/superpowers/.DS_Store export-ignore

# Editor/OS junk, never published.
**/.DS_Store export-ignore
